<td width=25% valign=top><font size=-1>
ENGLISH TRANSLATION<br>
<br>
<center><b>The clog-maker</b></center><br>
<br>
1. - Father, mother, What, do you mean, <br>
A splendid match I could have been?<br>
<br>
2. Instead of choosing a lawyer,<br>
You gave me to a clog-maker.<br>
<br>
3. Whose hut one tidies up in vain:<br>
Its wooden window has no pane!<br>
<br>
4. Depending on the time of year,<br>
It has a red or green veneer [?] -<br> 
<br>
5. Fanny brings him a daily meal.<br>
No path! Gropes around a great deal.<br>
<br>
6. Leaning on a beech in the shade,<br>
Fanny perceives a grating blade.<br>
<br>
7. Grating saw, then adze chopping wood:<br>
The clogger is in a bad mood ...<br></font>
<br>
